00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
European Union leaders meet to address a 360 billion euros trade deficit with China while setting the block's next 7-year budget and Ukraine's support. This is Omni View, episode 206. European Union heads of government gathered in Brussels for a summit expected to last two days. The agenda includes measures to reduce the block's trade deficit with China, which reached 360 billion euros last year. Further support for Ukraine forms another core item, and leaders will negotiate the next 7-year budget.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.620
year budget running from 2028 to 2034. Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky is scheduled

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.640
